<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8"/>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"/>
  <title><%= article.title %> — Modern Search</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #0a0a0f; --surface: #12121a; --surface2: #1a1a2a;
      --border: #2a2a3a; --accent: #6c63ff; --accent2: #38bdf8;
      --text: #e2e8f0; --muted: #64748b;
    }
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); min-height: 100vh; }

    nav {
      position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 100;
      background: rgba(10,10,15,0.85); backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding: 0 32px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 24px; height: 60px;
    }
    .nav-logo { font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); letter-spacing: -0.5px; text-decoration: none; }
    .nav-logo span { color: var(--accent2); }
    .nav-back {
      font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none;
      display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;
      transition: color 0.15s;
    }
    .nav-back:hover { color: var(--text); }

    .article-container {
      max-width: 760px; margin: 48px auto; padding: 0 24px;
    }

    .article-meta {
      display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }
    .category-badge {
      font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600;
      text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 4px;
    }
    .cat-Technology { background: rgba(56,189,248,0.15); color: var(--accent2); }
    .cat-Security   { background: rgba(239,68,68,0.12);  color: #f87171; }
    .cat-Research   { background: rgba(251,191,36,0.12); color: #fbbf24; }
    .meta-date, .meta-read { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); }

    h1 {
      font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.3;
      color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 16px;
    }
    .article-summary {
      font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7;
      border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
      padding-left: 16px; margin-bottom: 32px;
    }
    .author-row {
      display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;
      padding: 16px 20px; background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px;
      margin-bottom: 36px;
    }
    .author-avatar {
      width: 40px; height: 40px; border-radius: 50%;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2));
      display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700; color: #fff;
    }
    .author-name { font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600; }
    .author-label { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--muted); }

    .article-body {
      font-size: 0.97rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;
    }
    .article-body p { margin-bottom: 18px; }
    .article-body h2 {
      font-size: 1.3rem; color: var(--text); margin: 32px 0 12px;
    }
    .article-body code {
      background: var(--surface2); border: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: 4px;
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--accent2);
    }

    .tags-row { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 32px 0 48px; }
    .tag {
      font-size: 0.78rem; padding: 4px 12px;
      background: var(--surface2); color: var(--muted);
      border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px;
      text-decoration: none; transition: all 0.15s;
    }
    .tag:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }

    /* Related */
    .related-section h2 {
      font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted);
      margin-bottom: 16px;
      text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; font-size: 0.75rem;
    }
    .related-card {
      background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 18px;
      text-decoration: none; display: block; margin-bottom: 12px;
      transition: border-color 0.2s, transform 0.2s;
    }
    .related-card:hover { border-color: var(--accent); transform: translateX(4px); }
    .related-title { font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 4px; }
    .related-meta  { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--muted); }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<nav>
  <a class="nav-logo" href="/search">Modern<span>Search</span></a>
  <a class="nav-back" href="javascript:history.back()">← Back to results</a>
</nav>

<div class="article-container">

  <div class="article-meta">
    <span class="category-badge cat-<%= article.category %>"><%= article.category %></span>
    <span class="meta-date"><%= article.date %></span>
    <span class="meta-read">⏱ <%= article.readTime %> min read</span>
  </div>

  <h1><%= article.title %></h1>

  <div class="article-summary"><%= article.summary %></div>

  <div class="author-row">
    <div class="author-avatar"><%= article.author[0] %></div>
    <div>
      <div class="author-name"><%= article.author %></div>
      <div class="author-label">Contributing Researcher</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="article-body">
    <p>
      In today's rapidly evolving threat landscape, understanding the mechanics of this topic is
      essential for any security professional. This article provides an in-depth technical breakdown
      for practitioners at all levels.
    </p>
    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>
      <%= article.summary %> The implications of this go far beyond surface-level understanding —
      practitioners who grasp the underlying model are consistently better equipped to design
      defensive architectures.
    </p>
    <p>
      Key areas to consider include input validation, context-aware output encoding, and the role of
      browser security policies. The interplay between <code>Content-Security-Policy</code> headers
      and template engine escaping is particularly important in modern Node.js stacks.
    </p>
    <h2>Key Findings</h2>
    <p>
      Research in this area consistently demonstrates that the most effective mitigations are those
      applied as close to the output sink as possible. Relying solely on input sanitisation is
      insufficient — defence-in-depth requires encoding at every context boundary.
    </p>
    <p>
      <% var tagList = article.tags.map(t => '#' + t).join(', '); %>
      The tags associated with this article — <code><%= tagList %></code> — represent
      the core competency areas required to fully understand this subject matter.
    </p>
    <h2>Conclusion</h2>
    <p>
      The security community continues to develop better tooling, but fundamentals remain unchanged.
      Automated patch revalidation frameworks — such as those built around dynamic and static
      analysis — offer the highest assurance that fixes genuinely close the reported vulnerability
      rather than just masking symptoms.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="tags-row">
    <% article.tags.forEach(tag => { %>
    <a href="/search?q=<%= tag %>" class="tag">#<%= tag %></a>
    <% }) %>
  </div>

  <% if (related.length > 0) { %>
  <div class="related-section">
    <h2>Related Articles</h2>
    <% related.forEach(r => { %>
    <a class="related-card" href="/article/<%= r.id %>">
      <div class="related-title"><%= r.title %></div>
      <div class="related-meta"><%= r.author %> · <%= r.date %> · ⏱ <%= r.readTime %> min</div>
    </a>
    <% }) %>
  </div>
  <% } %>

</div>
</body>
</html>
